TraSH (TraSH Replaces Another SHell) is a POSIX-style shell written in C.

Instead of walking an abstract syntax tree, every command line is compiled
ahead of time to a small bytecode which a VM then executes. Run `trash -d`
to start a session that prints the bytecode of each command before running it.

Builtins: cd echo env exec exit export false logout pwd readonly return set
          true type unset help
Features: pipelines, && ||, ( subshells ), redirections < > >> and <<,
          $VAR and $? expansion, single and double quotes.
